      "writtenOn": "2020-10-07T16:25:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could you elaborate about the file type?  I\u0027m not aware of it.  Can Play generate the fs-verity signature for the file?  Package manager actually requires all (or none) installed files to have fs-verity consistently (at least in the regular flow, I know incremental has some special code).\n\nAlso note that we can\u0027t simply put a certificate into .fs-verity keyring.  Since fs-verity honors any key in the key ring, we need to keep the weakest key strong.",
      "parentUuid": "b8d49e86_6889e977",
      "revId": "7175461df5b351b97230d2168fbb458193edbb98",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
